  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "Despite achieving a positive gross P&L (+\u20b915.49), the strategy suffered a net loss of \u20b9-38.01 due to severe fee drag (\u20b953.50) across stagnant mid-day entries (11:05\u201314:10 IST) in low-beta heavyweights (ITC, AXISBANK, ICICIBANK, TATASTEEL) that failed to reach the 1.10% target and decayed into EOD_SQUARE_OFF. Simultaneously, an overly aggressive 2.85x volume sweep threshold triggered late entries at local climax exhaustion points (such as TATASTEEL stopping out within 5 minutes), where the maximum 0.75% stop-loss floor magnified single-trade drawdowns.",
    "learning": "In Indian NSE large-cap cash equities, extreme volume multipliers (>2.5x) after the morning opening drive frequently signal retail exhaustion rather than institutional continuation; pairing moderate volume confirmation with tighter stop-loss floors and realistic intraday targets prevents EOD time-decay and neutralizes statutory fee drag on small-capital accounts.",
    "parameter_patch": {
      "min_target_pct": 0.95,
      "min_sweep_vol_multiplier": 2.1,
      "breakeven_trigger_r": 0.85,
      "min_sl_pct": 0.55
    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #39 Post-Mortem & Parameter Mutation\nIn Cycle #39, the DeepSeek V4.1 Flash out-of-sample run generated positive gross alpha (+\u20b915.49) across 15 trades but closed net negative (\u20b9-38.01, PF 0.74) entirely due to transaction cost drag (\u20b953.50) and wide stop-loss hits on climax entries. Forensics revealed two core microstructure flaws: (1) `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` at 2.85x forced entries at the peak of exhaustion candles (e.g., TATASTEEL reversing to hit stop-loss within 5 minutes), and (2) `min_target_pct` at 1.10% proved overly ambitious for mid-day large-cap setups (ITC, AXISBANK, ICICIBANK), causing profitable intraday excursions to stall and exit at `EOD_SQUARE_OFF` for net fee losses. For Cycle #40, we are recalibrating `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` down to **2.10x** to capture institutional sweeps earlier in the impulse, tightening `min_sl_pct` from 0.75% to **0.55%** to cap downside on false breakouts, and lowering `min_target_pct` to **0.95%** (while retaining `breakeven_trigger_r` at **0.85R**) to convert stagnant EOD square-offs into realized target wins."
